Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:30:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cores: a tone mapping method of a reference display (BT.2390)

Kodi brings an HDR10 picture to an output that takes no HDR with one of its
own tone mapping methods (Reinhard, ACES or Hable, its default). A method is
added: "Reference (BT.2390)", the bridge's mapping of a reference display
(the BT.2390 curve guided by the stream's HDR10 metadata, the perceptual
gamut mapping into BT.709, HDR reference white at the display's white),
which the next commit draws with. Kodi's methods stay as they are, in the
video settings of the player and in the action that cycles through them.

It is the default: Kodi's default was Hable, and a Hable saved before this
method existed is taken for that default and becomes this one, once; the
file then says so (hadestonemap), and Hable chosen again stays. Where the
bridge does not draw a picture, Kodi's own shader draws it with Hable.

The label is a core string in English (#39827), translated in Estuary
(#31714: es_es, es_ar, es_mx), as the other strings of Hades.

Compiled in syntax-only mode and read; not run.
